<b>Not a Shred of Regret
With My Dried Sardines</b>

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.800
Thank you.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.140
So sleepy...

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:15.120
Huh?

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.920
<b>Incoming Call</b>

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.920
<b>Yuu</b>

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:18.920
Oh, it's just Yuu.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:20.750
Yeah?

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.190
<i>Hey, Bro? Where are you right now?</i>

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.580
<i>You may be in college, but you 
shouldn't be out partying all night.</i>

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:30.420
Excuse you. I just finished 
my night shift at the izakaya.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:31.310
<i>Oh.</i>

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.980
<i>Well, want me to leave some food out for you?</i>

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.780
<i>You have morning classes, right?</i>

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:39.740
Ugh, I'm so sleepy. 
I might just skip first period.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:01.610
<i>Hey, Bro?</i>

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.200
<i>Hello?</i>

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.870
<i>Are you there?</i>

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.750
<i>Hello, are you there?</i>

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:14.060
I'll have some ramen for breakfast, 
and then I'll go to class.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:14.060
<b>Amazing!

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:14.060
<b>Open
24 Hours</b>

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.560
<b>Brother</b>

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.560
<i>I'm suddenly feeling awake.</i>

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.180
What are you talking about?

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.570
Are there even any places
open at this hour?

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:23.100
There are.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:27.000
I just got a whiff of dried 
sardines off of a beautiful girl.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:32.960
<i>Bro, you really are tired.</i>

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:35.780
<i>You need to get some rest.</i>

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.280
<i>Are you listening? Bro—</i>

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:44.740
<b>Thank You</b>

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:43.680
Welcome.

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:52.020
Eating ramen for breakfast is a common 
practice in Shizuoka and Fukushima.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.600
And now, morning ramen 
has been made into candy.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.440
<b>Morning Ramen</b>

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.440
<b>Salt</b>

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.460
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:05.450
<b>Hiyashi</b>

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.100
It's so hot.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:19.210
Argh, it's so hot!

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.880
It's way too hot!

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:22.680
Hot, hot, hot, hot, hot, hot!

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.520
What, you want me to take everything off?!

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.370
Pipe down.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.630
Nope, nope, nope, nope, nope!

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:25.630
You're making it worse.

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:28.270
I want some juice or ice cream!

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:29.640
I'll agree to that.

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:33.830
Doesn't it feel like all we're 
eating lately is cold food?

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:38.680
Yeah, yesterday it was 90-Ice, 
and the day before that...

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.000
The frozen yogurt stand, right?

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:45.040
Yeah, that's it. And before that...
what was it again?

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.690
Either way, our diet is way too unbalanced.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:50.330
The heat has sapped my energy. 
I can't walk another step.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:53.990
Me, either. And I don't feel like 
eating anything except cold stuff.

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:55.140
Yeah.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:56.620
So, want to go anywhere today?

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.410
Well...

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.300
Koizumi-san!

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.090
Huh?

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:10.800
Hey, Koizumi-san!

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:13.600
Let's go grab something cold together!

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:14.350
Okay? Okay?

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:15.260
So overbearing...

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:16.240
No, thank you.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:22.020
I'm going to get some ramen.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:25.780
When it's this hot?

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.240
I know you're into ramen, but <i>today</i>? Really?!

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:31.910
It's admirable, in a sense.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:34.500
Having hot ramen in the middle of summer...

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.680
I-I'll go have ramen with you!

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.380
I'll go with you, Koizumi-san!

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.620
You're a mess of tears and sweat!

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:41.960
No, thank you.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:46.410
Also, you seem to have the wrong idea.

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:50.180
I'm not having regular ramen today.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:54.560
I'm having hiyashi ramen.

00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:58.480
Hiyashi... ramen?

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:01.150
What is that, exactly?

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:07.540
So Yuu ended up going with Koizumi.

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:10.990
I'm actually kind of curious 
about hiyashi ramen myself.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:13.480
Well, it wouldn't fog up your glasses.

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:14.490
Lay off.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:15.490
<b>No ice cubes.</b>

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.330
But you know, when I eat out in summer,

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:16.240
<b>No ice cubes.</b>

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:16.990
<b>No ice cubes.</b>

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.740
I usually can't order much cold stuff.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:21.000
Huh? Why not?

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:24.760
Usually, restaurants have their 
AC going full blast in the summer.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:33.890
<b>Feels cold the entire year</b>

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:27.080
So I go to Starbucks for a Frappuccino,

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:31.200
but by the time I reach the front of the line, 
I'm so cold, I just order a hot coffee.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:33.890
You're pretty high-maintenance, huh?

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:38.960
Anyway, it seems like there are
all kinds of hiyashi ramen flavors.

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:40.600
Like what? Let me see!

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:44.000
When I heard "cold noodles,"
I expected something like reimen,

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.750
but this looks totally different.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.280
Wow! What are these?

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:49.050
They almost look like parfaits!

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:51.320
The glass bowls look so cold.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:54.410
Hey, they've even got a chilled 
version of tantanmen, my favorite!

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.620
I want some!

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:59.080
Why don't you have some spicy ramen, 
too? I bet it'll warm you up.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.540
I have a weak stomach, so I can't.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:04.440
If I ate something that spicy, 
the next day, I'd be like...

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:07.340
Look, they've got hiyashi ramen here, too!

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.340
Chilled Tantanmen

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.340
Chilled Tomato Gelée Noodles

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:10.130
So, dinner...

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:11.590
Want to eat here?

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:16.570
But didn't you say that air conditioning
makes you not want to eat cold food?

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:18.510
Don't worry about that.

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.670
Starting this year, I've got this.

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:23.520
So you <i>will</i> eat it.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:26.020
<b>Kanda Suzuran Street</b>

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:33.530
Hiyashi ramen originally came 
from Yamagata Prefecture.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:40.150
The dish was invented over sixty years ago,
and not in a ramen shop, but a soba shop.

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:41.290
Really?

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:43.760
They were making ramen in a soba shop?

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:46.260
And it's been around for 
quite a long time, too.

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:48.000
Thank you for waiting!

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:53.130
One bright red tomato sour ramen 
and one tsuttai ramen.

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:56.760
Wow, there's ice in it!

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:00.560
The bowl feels so cool!

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:05.140
It doesn't smell as strong as regular ramen.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:10.290
Anyway, hiyashi ramen is totally 
different from hiyashi chuuka, huh?

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:13.150
It has more soup, and it 
doesn't smell like vinegar.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:17.440
In Hokkaido, they call
hiyashi chuuka "hiyashi ramen."

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:21.920
And in the Kansai region,
they call hiyashi chuuka "reimen."

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.540
That seems so complicated.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:27.770
So is this soup the regular 
hot soup, but chilled?

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:31.690
Ramen soup generally has 
a lot of animal fat in it,

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:34.550
so if you were to do that,
you'd end up with lumps of fat.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.440
Oh, yeah...

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:39.200
The main ingredient is pork or chicken bones.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:41.660
Which is why you use plenty 
of vegetable-based fat

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:43.820
to maintain the body,
and then make separate

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:49.350
batches of stock and sauce for the hiyashi
ramen in order to adjust the flavor properly.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.950
Since the process is so complicated,

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:56.060
in many places, the dish is only 
offered during summer months.

00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:58.070
That does sound like a lot of work.

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:00.830
It is strictly a seasonal summer pleasure.

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:02.050
Well, shall we?

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:02.830
Yes!

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:05.830
Time to eat.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.720
Force of habit...

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:16.340
That's right. It's cold.

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:18.840
Thank you for waiting!

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:20.910
This looks delicious.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:22.600
This is great!

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:25.180
Let's eat!

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:35.810
So cold!

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.620
Thank you for the food!

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:46.600
Eating cold food always 
makes me crave hot food.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:48.610
Where should I go next?

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:51.980
I'll go with you!

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:57.000
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:02.360
<b>Museum</b>

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.540
Look at that girl in the yukata!

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:06.670
She's so cute.

00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:08.620
Was there a festival today?

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:12.000
Hmm... Doesn't look like it.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:15.980
So... where do you think she's going?

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:35.150
<b>For Narutobashi</b>

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:28.720
Little girl, are you lost?

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:30.700
Are you okay?

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:33.370
<b>Mommy, mommy!</b>

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.710
<b>Shina Sobaya</b>

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:43.050
Welcome!

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:44.880
Party of two?

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:48.660
No, I'm alone...

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:52.850
<b>Mommy?</b>

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:55.100
<i>German?</i>

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:58.100
<b>No, my name is Koizumi.</b>

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:16.250
<b>Stare...</b>

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:19.330
<b>What's your name?</b>

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:20.670
<b>Hannah.</b>

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:24.590
<b>I've lost my mommy.</b>

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:27.090
<b>Lost Child Situation</b>

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:31.030
<b>Mommy...</b>

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:32.180
<b>Don't worry.</b>

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:36.470
I'll tell the staff, and they'll
look for your mother.

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:38.290
Thank you for waiting!

00:14:39.470 --> 00:14:41.020
One soy sauce ramen.

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:43.470
Excuse me, this girl...

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:45.840
...needs her own plate?

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:46.810
Of course. One moment.

00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:48.930
No, I mean—

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:55.440
Here's a child's bowl.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:56.420
Um...

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:02.630
<b>Tremble</b>

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:02.630
<b>Grumble
Gurgle</b>

00:14:58.460 --> 00:14:59.710
<b>I'm hungry...</b>

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:07.630
I guess we'll look for your 
mother after we finish eating.

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:09.820
Let's eat together.

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:17.020
If I had known, I would've 
ordered a half portion extra.

00:15:17.510 --> 00:15:25.230
Food courts like this offer half portions
so you can try many different things.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.690
Mini Salt
Limited Edition Char Siu Ramen

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:25.230
Mini Soy Sauce 
Limited Edition Char Siu Ramen

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:25.230
Mini Salt Ramen

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:29.610
Still, it would take too long 
if I ordered one of those now.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:31.400
<b>Go ahead.</b>

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.410
<b>Thank you!</b>

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:37.240
<b>This looks so good!</b>

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:41.600
Ramen has achieved a certain 
popularity recently in Germany.

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:42.540
Oh...

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.210
<b>Oh, one moment, please.</b>

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:46.540
Here you go.

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:49.490
These are vital when you're 
eating ramen in a yukata.

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:52.170
Pin your sleeves down with these.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.550
<b>Yay!</b>

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:58.910
All right, let's eat.

00:15:58.910 --> 00:15:59.600
Bitte.

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:00.810
<b>Thank you!</b>

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:02.560
L-L-L-Let's eat!

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:11.860
<b>Yummy!</b>

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:26.500
<b>Sano Minoru</b>

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:25.090
This is good.

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:29.960
Thank you for the food.

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:32.510
Thank you for the food.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:35.670
Thank you!

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:41.420
That was delicious.

00:16:41.420 --> 00:16:43.000
Thank you!

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:44.770
Delicious!

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:50.670
So, now what?

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:06.960
<b>Uh...</b>

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:15.010
<b>Hannah!</b>

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:18.390
<b>Where are you, Hannah?</b>

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:20.470
<b>Hannah?</b>

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:21.120
Hannah?

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:21.680
<b>Mommy!</b>

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:21.720
<b>Mommy!</b>

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:23.890
<b>Mommy!</b>

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:26.230
<b>Hannah!</b>

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.400
<b>Mommy!</b>

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:30.110
<b>Hannah!</b>

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.240
<b>Mommy!</b>

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:37.410
<b>It's okay. Don't cry.</b>

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:38.820
<b>Where were you?</b>

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:41.450
<b>Koizumi helped me!</b>

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:51.750
Koizumi-san, thank you so much.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:54.160
Please, think nothing of it.

00:17:54.160 --> 00:17:55.730
Ah, ja!

00:17:57.650 --> 00:17:58.750
Here you go.

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:01.410
I'll give you this ramen 
voucher to thank you.

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:03.560
It's a delicious German ramen.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.930
Please try it! The restaurant is right there.

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:10.600
It would be rude to refuse.

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:12.960
I'll accept it, then.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:15.440
Thank you very much.

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:18.780
<b>Thank you! Bye-bye!</b>

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:35.440
Germany, huh?

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:38.390
Welcome.

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:41.060
Thank you for waiting.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:44.600
One Muku Zweite Ramen.

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:47.980
<b>Bacon</b>

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:47.980
<b>Speck
(German bacon)</b>

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:47.980
<b>Sauerkraut
(fermented cabbage)</b>

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:47.980
<b>Spices</b>

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:52.350
Time to eat.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:14.920
So this... is Germany.

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:30.930
Lecker!

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:44.060
I thoroughly enjoyed the German ramen.

